{"id": "EUVD-2026-95807", "enisaUuid": "d5cfe7b5-4c20-3537-916f-e0475884a3fa", "description": "Xerial snappy-java before 1.1.10.9 contains an unbounded memory allocation vulnerability that allows attackers to exhaust JVM memory by declaring a large uncompressed length in compressed input. Attackers can supply a few crafted bytes to Snappy.uncompress, uncompressString, SnappyInputStream or SnappyFramedInputStream to force allocations up to 2 GB, causing OutOfMemoryError and denial of service.", "datePublished": "2026-10-09T14:33:29", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T16:51:17", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/xerial/snappy-java/security/advisories/GHSA-q233-g92q-qxp6", "https://github.com/xerial/snappy-java/commit/943c6043a292568575e8347af4507d015e802c75", "https://github.com/xerial/snappy-java/releases/tag/v1.1.10.9", "https://github.com/xerial/snappy-java/blob/v1.1.10.8/src/main/java/org/xerial/snappy/Snappy.java#L517", "https://github.com/xerial/snappy-java", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/xerial-snappy-java-before-1.1.10.9-unbounded-memory-allocation-denial-of-service"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-108106", "GHSA-94x4-5g3f-jjxp"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.37, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "7b687d81-0dc7-3df7-9ebc-5d521a2764f2", "product": {"name": "snappy-java", "vendor": {"name": "xerial"}}, "product_version": "0 <1.1.10.9"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "789f539e-7d0e-3f74-9feb-8f6f1f29c701", "vendor": {"name": "xerial"}}], "isExploited": false}